WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.072
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book two.

2
00:00:05.372 --> 00:00:08.816
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.116 --> 00:00:14.717
Unit sixteen: Rainforests. In this unit, you will explain why rainforests are important.

4
00:00:15.717 --> 00:00:16.671
Rainforest.

5
00:00:17.371 --> 00:00:20.381
Rainforest means a thick forest with a lot of rain.

6
00:00:20.681 --> 00:00:22.913
The Amazon is a huge rainforest.

7
00:00:23.613 --> 00:00:25.882
Your turn. Say: Rainforest.

8
00:00:28.582 --> 00:00:29.664
Rainforest.

9
00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:31.338
Tree.

10
00:00:32.038 --> 00:00:34.722
Tree means a tall plant with a trunk and branches.

11
00:00:35.022 --> 00:00:37.242
Some trees are 60 metres tall.

12
00:00:37.942 --> 00:00:40.223
Your turn. Say: Tree.

13
00:00:42.923 --> 00:00:43.553
Tree.

14
00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:45.447
Animal.

15
00:00:46.147 --> 00:00:50.224
Animal means a living thing that can move, like a dog or a bird.

16
00:00:50.524 --> 00:00:52.582
Thousands of animals live there.

17
00:00:53.282 --> 00:00:55.946
Your turn. Say: Animal.

18
00:00:58.646 --> 00:00:59.450
Animal.

19
00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:01.254
Rain.

20
00:01:01.954 --> 00:01:04.255
Rain means water that falls from clouds.

21
00:01:04.555 --> 00:01:06.253
It rains almost every day.

22
00:01:06.953 --> 00:01:09.640
Your turn. Say: Rain.

23
00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:13.097
Rain.

24
00:01:14.083 --> 00:01:14.957
Cut down.

25
00:01:15.657 --> 00:01:18.016
Cut down means to make a tree fall by cutting it.

26
00:01:18.316 --> 00:01:20.107
People cut down trees for wood.

27
00:01:20.807 --> 00:01:23.622
Your turn. Say: Cut down.

28
00:01:26.322 --> 00:01:27.346
Cut down.

29
00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:29.258
Oxygen.

30
00:01:29.958 --> 00:01:32.852
Oxygen means the gas in the air that we need to breathe.

31
00:01:33.152 --> 00:01:34.524
Trees give us oxygen.

32
00:01:35.224 --> 00:01:37.447
Your turn. Say: Oxygen.

33
00:01:40.147 --> 00:01:41.090
Oxygen.

34
00:01:42.083 --> 00:01:42.899
Protect.

35
00:01:43.599 --> 00:01:45.262
Protect means to keep safe.

36
00:01:45.562 --> 00:01:47.294
We need to protect the forest.

37
00:01:47.994 --> 00:01:50.263
Your turn. Say: Protect.

38
00:01:52.963 --> 00:01:53.790
Protect.

39
00:01:54.783 --> 00:01:55.877
Species.

40
00:01:56.577 --> 00:01:59.633
Species means a group of similar animals or plants.

41
00:01:59.933 --> 00:02:02.444
Many species live only in rainforests.

42
00:02:03.144 --> 00:02:06.051
Your turn. Say: Species.

43
00:02:08.751 --> 00:02:09.799
Species.

44
00:02:10.783 --> 00:02:12.945
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:13.245 --> 00:02:15.872
Sreypich, why are rainforests important?

46
00:02:17.183 --> 00:02:20.088
Trees give us oxygen, so they are very important.

47
00:02:21.383 --> 00:02:22.617
What lives in them?

48
00:02:23.917 --> 00:02:27.124
Many species, because there is a lot of food and rain.

49
00:02:28.417 --> 00:02:29.650
What's the problem?

50
00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:34.389
People cut down trees, so animals lose their homes.

51
00:02:35.683 --> 00:02:38.252
Grammar focus: Because and so.

52
00:02:38.552 --> 00:02:40.760
Trees give oxygen, so they are important.

53
00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:43.910
'Because' gives the reason. 'So' gives the result.

54
00:02:44.917 --> 00:02:47.453
Now read and listen. The Lungs of the Earth.

55
00:02:47.753 --> 00:02:50.345
Rainforests have tall trees and lots of rain.

56
00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:55.751
Many animal species live there because there is food all year.

57
00:02:57.050 --> 00:03:01.163
Trees give us oxygen, so rainforests are called the lungs of the Earth.

58
00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:05.018
But people cut down forests for wood and farms.

59
00:03:06.317 --> 00:03:10.220
We need to protect rainforests, so animals can keep their homes.

60
00:03:11.517 --> 00:03:14.111
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:14.411 --> 00:03:17.328
Trees give oxygen, blank they are important.

62
00:03:17.628 --> 00:03:20.828
A, so. B, because. C, but.

63
00:03:24.817 --> 00:03:26.990
The answer is A: so.

64
00:03:28.483 --> 00:03:31.238
Animals live there blank there is food.

65
00:03:31.538 --> 00:03:35.017
A, because. B, so. C, or.

66
00:03:39.017 --> 00:03:40.912
The answer is A: because.

67
00:03:42.417 --> 00:03:44.648
The gas in the air that we breathe is blank.

68
00:03:44.948 --> 00:03:48.381
A, oxygen. B, rain. C, species.

69
00:03:52.383 --> 00:03:54.708
The answer is A: oxygen.

70
00:03:56.217 --> 00:03:59.647
Now it's your turn to speak. Why are rainforests important?

71
00:04:04.947 --> 00:04:11.198
Rainforests are important because they give us oxygen. Many animals live there, so we must protect them.

72
00:04:11.498 --> 00:04:13.440
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:14.450 --> 00:04:18.112
Great work today! You learned eight new words and because and so.

74
00:04:18.412 --> 00:04:22.632
Today's value is caring for nature. Care for plants, birds and our planet.

75
00:04:22.932 --> 00:04:25.759
See you in Unit seventeen. Goodbye!

76
00:04:26.059 --> 00:04:28.850
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

